.TH HACKTV "1" "October 2026" "hacktv 20261012" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hacktv \- analogue TV transmitter for the HackRF and other SDRs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hacktv
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,input \/\fR[\fI\,input\/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR <target>
Set the output device or file, Default: hackrf
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR <name>
Set the television mode. Default: i
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-modes\fR
List available modes and exit.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-samplerate\fR <value>
Set the sample rate in Hz. Default: 20.25MHz
.TP
\fB\-\-pixelrate\fR <value>
Set the video pixel rate in Hz. Default: Sample rate
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-level\fR <value>
Set the output level. Default: 1.0
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-deviation\fR <value>
Override the mode's FM peak deviation. (Hz)
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-gamma\fR <value>
Override the mode's gamma correction value.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interlace\fR
Update image each field instead of each frame.
.TP
\fB\-\-fit\fR <mode>
Set fit mode. (Disabled in this version)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-aspect\fR <value>
Set the minimum aspect ratio for fit mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-aspect\fR <value>
Set the maximum aspect ratio for fit mode.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-repeat\fR
Repeat the inputs forever.
.TP
\fB\-\-shuffle\fR
Randomly shuffle the inputs.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-position\fR <value>
Set start position of video in minutes.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-\-logo\fR <path>
Overlay picture logo over video.
.TP
\fB\-\-timestamp\fR
Overlay video timestamp over video.
.TP
\fB\-\-teletext\fR <path>
Enable teletext output. (625 line modes only)
.TP
\fB\-\-wss\fR <mode>
Set WSS output. Defaults to auto. (625 line modes only)
.TP
\fB\-\-letterbox\fR
Letterboxes widescreen content on 4:3 screen.
.TP
\fB\-\-pillarbox\fR
Zooms widescreen content to fill 4:3 screen.
.TP
\fB\-\-videocrypt\fR <mode>
Enable Videocrypt I scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-enableemm\fR <serial>
Enable a Videocrypt card. Use first 8 digits of serial number.
.TP
\fB\-\-disableemm\fR <serial>
Disable a Videocrypt card. Use first 8 digits of serial number.
.TP
\fB\-\-videocrypt2\fR <mode>
Enable Videocrypt II scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-videocrypts\fR <mode>
Enable Videocrypt S scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-showserial\fR
Displays serial number of the Videocrypt card.
.TP
\fB\-\-findkey\fR
Attempt to find keys of PPV Videocrypt card.
.TP
\fB\-\-syster\fR <mode>
Enable Nagravision Syster scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-d11\fR <mode>
Enable Discret 11 scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-d14\fR
Enable Discret 14 scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-cablecrypt\-tvcabo\fR
Enable Cablecrypt (TV Cabo) scrambling. (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-systercnr\fR <mode>
Enable Syster cut and rotate scrambling (***INCOMPLETE***). (PAL only)
.TP
\fB\-\-systeraudio\fR
Invert the audio spectrum when using Syster, Syster CnR or D11 scrambling.
.TP
\fB\-\-acp\fR
Enable Analogue Copy Protection signal.
.TP
\fB\-\-vits\fR
Enable VITS test signals.
.TP
\fB\-\-cc608\fR
Enable CEA/EIA\-608 closed\-caption pass through.
.TP
\fB\-\-vitc\fR
Enable VITC time code.
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\fR
Enable experimental VSB modulation filter.
.TP
\fB\-\-nocolour\fR
Disable the colour subcarrier (PAL, SECAM, NTSC only).
.TP
\fB\-\-s\-video\fR
Output colour subcarrier on second channel.
(PAL, NTSC, SECAM baseband modes only).
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\fR <value>
Adjust volume. Takes floats as argument.
.TP
\fB\-\-noaudio\fR
Suppress all audio subcarriers.
.TP
\fB\-\-nonicam\fR
Disable the NICAM subcarrier if present.
.TP
\fB\-\-a2stereo\fR
Enable Zweikanalton / A2 Stereo, disables NICAM.
.TP
\fB\-\-single\-cut\fR
Enable D/D2\-MAC single cut video scrambling.
.TP
\fB\-\-double\-cut\fR
Enable D/D2\-MAC double cut video scrambling.
.TP
\fB\-\-eurocrypt\fR <mode>
Enable Eurocrypt conditional access for D/D2\-MAC.
.TP
\fB\-\-ec\-mat\-rating\fR <rating>
Enable Eurocrypt maturity rating.
.TP
\fB\-\-ec\-ppv\fR <pnum,cost>
Enable Eurocrypt PPV.
.TP
\fB\-\-nodate\fR
Set the date verification bit in Eurocrypt ECMs.
.TP
\fB\-\-scramble\-audio\fR
Scramble audio data when using D/D2\-MAC modes.
.TP
\fB\-\-chid\fR <id>
Set the channel ID (D/D2\-MAC).
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-table\-1\fR
Set permutation key table 1 in Syster.
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-table\-2\fR
Set permutation key table 2 in Syster.
.TP
\fB\-\-subtitles\fR <stream idx>
Enable subtitles. Takes an optional argument.
.HP
\fB\-\-tx\-subtitles\fR <stream id> Enable subtitles on teletext page 888.
.TP
\fB\-\-downmix\fR
Downmix 5.1 audio to 2.0.
.TP
\fB\-\-showecm\fR
Show input and output control words for scrambled modes.
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-stereo\fR
Use stereo audio (D/D2\-MAC). (Default)
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-mono\fR
Use mono audio (D/D2\-MAC).
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-high\-quality\fR
Use high quality 32 kHz audio (D/D2\-MAC).
(Default)
.HP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-medium\-quality\fR Use medium quality 16 kHz audio (D/D2\-MAC).
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-companded\fR
Use companded audio compression (D/D2\-MAC).
(Default)
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-linear\fR
Use linear audio. (D/D2\-MAC).
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-l1\-protection\fR
Use first level protection (D/D2\-MAC).
(Default)
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\-audio\-l2\-protection\fR
Use second level protection (D/D2\-MAC).
.TP
\fB\-\-sis\fR <mode>
Enable Sound\-in\-Syncs (dcsis only)
.TP
\fB\-\-swap\-iq\fR
Swap the I and Q channels to invert the spectrum.
Applied before offset and passthru. (Complex modes only).
.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR <value>
Add a frequency offset in Hz (Complex modes only).
.TP
\fB\-\-passthru\fR <file>
Read and add an int16 complex signal.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-bb\-file\fR <file>
Read the active video from a raw int16 baseband file.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-bb\-blanking\fR <value>
Blanking level of the raw baseband file. Default: 0
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-bb\-white\fR <value>
White level of the raw baseband file. Default: 32767
.TP
\fB\-\-cps\fR <file>
Replay a PLN/CPS test card file.
.TP
\fB\-\-invert\-video\fR
Invert the composite video signal sync and
white levels.
.TP
\fB\-\-secam\-field\-id\fR
Enable SECAM field identification.
.TP
\fB\-\-secam\-field\-id\-lines\fR <x> Set the number of lines per field used for SECAM field
identification. (1\-9, default: 9)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output a JSON array when used with \fB\-\-list\-modes\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version number and exit.
.PP
Input options
.TP
test:colourbars
Generate and transmit a test pattern.
.TP
test:pm5544
Transmit a PM5544 test pattern. (Default)
.TP
test:pm5644
Transmit a PM5644 (16:9) test pattern.
.TP
test:ueitm
Transmit a UEITM test pattern.
.TP
test:fubk
Transmit a FUBK test pattern.
.TP
ffmpeg:<file|url>
Decode and transmit a video file with ffmpeg.
.IP
If no valid input prefix is provided, ffmpeg: is assumed.
.IP
While a video is playing, Space pauses and resumes, and the right and
left arrow keys skip forward and back by 60 seconds.
.PP
ffmpeg input options
.TP
\fB\-\-ffmt\fR <format>
Force input file format.
.TP
\fB\-\-fopts\fR <option=value[:option2=value]>
Pass option(s) to ffmpeg.
.PP
HackRF output options
.HP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR hackrf[:<serial>] Open a HackRF for output.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-frequency\fR <value>
Set the RF frequency in Hz, 0MHz to 7250MHz.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-amp\fR
Enable the TX RF amplifier.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gain\fR <value>
Set the TX VGA (IF) gain, 0\-47dB. Default: 0dB
.IP
Only complex modes (RF) are supported by the HackRF.
Baseband modes are support with the addition of a HackDAC module.
.PP
SoapySDR output options
.HP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR soapysdr[:<opts>] Open a SoapySDR device for output.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-frequency\fR <value>
Set the RF frequency in Hz.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gain\fR <value>
Set the TX level. Default: 0dB
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-antenna\fR <name>
Set the antenna.
.PP
fl2k output options
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR fl2k[:<dev>]
Open an fl2k device for output.
.TP
\fB\-\-fl2k\-audio\fR <mode>
Audio mode (none, mono, stereo, spdif),
default: none
.IP
Each of the FL2K's three output channels can be used for:
.IP
Red: Baseband video / Complex I signal
Green: Complex Q signal / Analogue audio (Left) / Nothing
Blue: Analogue audio (Right/Mono) / Digital audio (S/PDIF) / Nothing
.IP
The 0.7v p\-p voltage level of the FL2K is too low to create a correct
composite video signal, it will appear too dark without amplification.
.IP
Digital S/PDIF audio is currently fixed at 16\-bit, 32 kHz. Not all
decoders work at this sample rate.
.IP
Analogue audio is limited to 8\-bits. The LSB is delta\-sigma modulated at
the FL2K sample rate with the lower 8\-bits of the 16\-bit audio and may be
recovered by using a low pass filter of ~16 kHz on the output.
.PP
File output options
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR file:<filename>
Open a file for output. Use \- for stdout.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR <type>
Set the file data type.
.PP
Supported file types:
.IP
uint8
int8
uint16
int16
int32
float
.IP
The default output is int16. The TV mode will determine if the output
is real or complex.
.IP
If no valid output prefix is provided, file: is assumed.
.PP
NOTE: The number of samples per line is rounded to the nearest integer,
which may result in a slight frame rate error.
.PP
For modes which include audio you also need to ensure the sample rate
is adequate to contain both the video signal and audio subcarriers.
.PP
16MHz works well with PAL modes, and 13.5MHz for NTSC modes.
.PP
20.25MHz is ideal for the D/D2\-MAC modes, but may not work with all hackrfs.
.PP
Teletext
.PP
Teletext is a digital information service transmitted within the VBI lines of
the video signal. Developed in the UK in the 1970s, it was used throughout
much of Europe until the end of analogue TV in the 2010s.
.PP
hacktv supports TTI files. The path can be either a single file or a
directory. All files in the directory will be loaded.
.PP
Raw packet sources are also supported with the raw:<source> path name.
The input is expected to be 42 byte teletext packets. Use \- for stdin.
.PP
Lines 7\-22 and 320\-335 are used, 16 lines per field.
.PP
Teletext support in hacktv is only compatible with 625 line PAL modes.
NTSC and SECAM variations exist and may be supported in the future.
.PP
WSS (Widescreen Signaling)
.PP
WSS provides a method to signal to a TV the intended aspect ratio of
the video. The following modes are supported:
.TP
4:3
= 4:3 video
.TP
14:9\-letterbox
= 14:9 video centred
.TP
14:9\-top
= 14:9 video at top
.TP
16:9\-letterbox
= 16:9 video centred
.TP
16:9\-top
= 16:9 video at top
.IP
16:9+\-letterbox = >16:9 video centred
14:9\-window     = 4:3 video with a 14:9 protected window
16:9            = 16:9 video (Anamorphic)
auto            = Automatically switch between 4:3 and 16:9 modes.
.PP
Currently only supported in 625 line modes. A 525 line variant exists and
may be supported in future.
.PP
Videocrypt I
.PP
A video scrambling system used by the Sky TV analogue satellite service in
the UK in the 1990s. Each line of the image is cut at a point determined by
a pseudorandom number generator, then the two parts are swapped.
.PP
hacktv supports the following modes:
.TP
free
= Free\-access, no subscription card is required to decode.
.TP
jstv
= A valid JSTV card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
sky02 \- sky06
= A valid Sky card of that series is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
sky07
= A valid Sky series 07 card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
sky09
= A valid Sky series 09 card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
sky09nano
= A valid Sky series 09 card with nanos enabled is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
sky10
= A valid Sky series 10 card is required to decode. Sample data from Sky One.
.TP
sky10ppv
= A valid Sky series 10 card with PPV enabled is required to decode.
.IP
Sample data from Tyson fight in 1996.
.TP
sky11
= A valid Sky series 11 card is required to decode. Sample data from MTV.
.TP
sky12
= A valid Sky series 12 card is required to decode. Sample data from Sky One.
.TP
skynz01
= A valid Sky New Zealand card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
skynz02
= A valid Sky New Zealand card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
tac1
= A valid TAC card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
tac2
= A valid TAC card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
dmx
= A valid DMX card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
scast
= A valid Sportscast card is required to decode. Random control words.
.TP
xtea
= Uses xtea encryption for control words. Needs Funcard programmed with
.IP
supplied hex files. Random control words.
.TP
ppv
= Memory cards, such as old phone cards, may work in this mode.
.PP
Videocrypt is only compatible with 625 line PAL modes. This version
works best when used with samples rates at multiples of 14MHz.
.PP
Enable/Disable EMM
.PP
This option attempts to switch on or off your card. Parameter is first 8 digits of your card number.
Supported in the sky06, sky07, sky09, sky09nano, skynz01, skynz02, tac1 and tac2 modes.
.PP
Videocrypt II
.PP
A variation of Videocrypt I used throughout Europe. The scrambling method is
identical to VC1, but has a higher VBI data rate.
.PP
hacktv supports the following modes:
.TP
free
= Free\-access, no subscription card is required to decode.
.TP
conditional
= A valid Multichoice card is required to decode. Random control words.
.PP
Videocrypt S
.PP
A variation of Videocrypt II used on the short lived BBC Select service. This
mode uses line\-shuffling rather than line cut\-and\-rotate.
.PP
hacktv supports the following modes:
.TP
free
= Free\-access, no subscription card is required to decode.
.IP
conditional = A new random CW every 32 frames, sent in bytes 19\-26 of the F9 messages. Needs a card that returns those bytes.
.PP
Audio inversion is not yet supported.
.PP
Nagravision Syster
.PP
Another video scrambling system used in the 1990s in Europe. The video lines
are vertically shuffled within a field.
.PP
hacktv supports the following modes (number in brackets indicates the permutation table):
.TP
premiere\-fa
= (1) A valid Premiere 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.TP
premiere\-ca
= (1) A valid Premiere 'key' is required to decode \- subscription level access.
.TP
cfrfa
= (2) A valid Canal+ France 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.TP
cfrca
= (2) A valid Canal+ France 'key' is required to decode \- subscription level access.
.TP
cplfa
= (1) A valid Canal+ Poland 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.TP
cesfa
= (1) A valid Canal+ Spain 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.TP
chorfa
= (2) A valid Canal+ Horizons 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.TP
ntvfa
= (2) A valid HTB+ Russia 'key' is required to decode \- free access.
.PP
By default, PAL providers use permutation table 1 and SECAM ones use table 2.
.PP
Discret 11
.PP
This scrambling system is a precursor to Syster in 1980s and mid\-1990s. Uses one of three
line delays to create a jagged effect. This will work with Syster decoders and dedicated Discret ones.
Syster decoder will require one of valid keys used in Syster (above).
.PP
Discret parameter requires one of the above modes specified.
.PP
Some decoders will invert the audio around 12.8 kHz. For these devices you need
to use the \fB\-\-systeraudio\fR option.
.PP
Eurocrypt
.PP
Conditional access (CA) system used by D/D2MAC services, M, S, S2 and 3DES versions are
supported.
.PP
hacktv supports the following modes:
.TP
bbcprime
= (M) A valid BBC Prime card is required to decode.
.TP
cplusfr
= (M) A valid Canal+ France (4:3) card is required to decode.
.TP
cplusfr169
= (M) A valid Canal+ France (16:9) card is required to decode.
.TP
ctv
= (M) A valid CTV card is required to decode.
.TP
filmnet
= (M) A valid FilmNet card is required to decode.
.TP
multivisio
= (M) A valid Multivisio card is required to decode.
.TP
tv3
= (M) A valid TV3 card is required to decode.
.TP
tv1000
= (M) A valid Viasat TV1000 card is required to decode.
.TP
tvcable
= (M) A valid TV Cable card is required to decode.
.TP
tvplus
= (M) A valid TV Plus (Netherlands) card is required to decode.
.TP
visiopass
= (M) A valid Visiopass card is required to decode.
.TP
teletv
= (S) A valid Tele\-TV card is required to decode.
.TP
nrk
= (S2) A valid NRK card is required to decode.
.TP
tv2
= (S2) A valid TV2 (Norway) card is required to decode.
.TP
ctvs
= (S2) A valid CTV card is required to decode.
.TP
eros
= (S2) A valid Eros card is required to decode.
.TP
rdv
= (S2) A valid RDV card is required to decode.
.TP
tvs
= (S2) A valid TVS (Denmark) card is required to decode.
.TP
cplus
= (3DES) A valid Canal+ Nordic card is required to decode.
.PP
MultiMac style cards can also be used.
